# Three real CLI scans over labeled source/context revisions; no provider or target code execution.
name: Source and context comparison across immutable revisions
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
shell: python3 @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_comparison.py @TMP_TARGET @ART/fixture
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | shell-ready
submit: runs diff context-base context-later
require-live-snap: 30 Threat model: changed | loaded-conditions
require-live-snap: 30 SEEN AGAIN | comparison-outcome
expect: [Findings]
expect: scan conditions differ
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
expect-not: loading
expect-not: missing findings.json
ask: Does the 120x36 comparison lead with the outcome, changed conditions and a visible way to inspect sources?
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 Base threat model: tm_ | recorded-contexts
expect: [Sources & context]
expect: Later threat model: tm_
expect: status: completed -> completed
expect-not: content:unknown
ask: Does Tab reveal the full source and context identities without losing the run pair?
resize: 80x24
live-snap: narrow-contexts
expect: Threat model: changed
ask: At 80x24, are full source and context values legible, with the active tab and paging affordance visible?
resize: 60x20
nav-mode:
keys: NPage
live-snap: comparison-details
expect: Later threat model:
keys: Tab
live-snap: compact-findings-return
expect: [Findings]
expect: SEEN AGAIN
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
ask: Can the operator return directly to the findings at 60x20 without scrolling through identifiers?
keys: Tab
live-snap: restored-source-scroll
expect: Later threat model:
ask: Does returning to Sources restore its reading position and leave both tabs reachable?
keys: g
keys: Tab
resize: 60x20
live-snap: compact-outcome
expect: [Findings]
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
ask: Is the 60x20 comparison understandable and navigable without truncated controls?
resize: 40x12
live-snap: smallest-outcome
expect: [Findings]
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
keys: G
live-snap: smallest-tail
expect: AWS Access Key
ask: At 40x12, can the operator reach the observation while the tabs remain visible?
keys: g
resize: 96x89
live-snap: tall-outcome
expect: SEEN AGAIN
ask: Does the tall viewport retain a coherent reading order without stretching the comparison into unrelated panels?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: wide-outcome
expect: SEEN AGAIN
ask: Does the wide viewport make the outcome, caveat and finding easy to scan?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: runs diff context-later context-dirty
require-live-snap: 30 SEEN AGAIN | dirty-outcome
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 30 Later threat model: explicitly no threat-model context | dirty-source-context
expect: status: completed -> completed
expect: main, dirty
expect: main, clean
expect-not: content:unknown
ask: Do these runs show the same full SHA with distinct content hashes and an explicit context omission, without implying a fix?
keys: C-c
